              "text": "As an AI, I am unable to directly purchase tickets, access your payment information, or make bookings on your behalf. However, I can provide you with the exact details, dates, and direct links you need to book your trip quickly.\n\n### 1. Confirm Your Dates\nBased on today's date of **Sunday, May 31, 2026**, \"next Friday\" typically refers to:\n* **Departure Date:** Friday, June 5, 2026 (or Friday, June 12, 2026, depending on your phrasing).\n* **Return Date:** You will need to select your preferred return date to Boston (for example, Sunday, June 7, 2026). \n\n### 2. Choose Your Train Service\nAmtrak offers two primary train options from **Boston South Station (BOS)** to **New York Moynihan Train Hall at Penn Station (NYP)**:\n* **Northeast Regional:** This is the standard service. It takes about **4 hours** and is the most cost-effective option. \n* **Acela (High-Speed):** This is Amtrak's premium high-speed train. It takes about **3.5 hours**, features fewer stops, and offers business/first-class seating.\n\n### 3. How to Book Your Return Ticket\nYou can secure your tickets in a few quick steps:\n\n* **Book Online:** Visit the official [Amtrak Booking Page](https://www.amtrak.com/).\n  1. Set your trip type to **Round-Trip**.\n  2. Input **Boston, MA (BOS)** as your origin and **New York, NY (NYP)** as your destination.\n  3. Select your departure date (e.g., June 5) and your return date.\n  4. Choose your preferred departure times and complete your payment.\n* **Book via Mobile App:** Download the **Amtrak App** on your smartphone. It is the easiest way to book, get live boarding gate updates, and show your e-ticket to the conductor.\n* **Book by Phone:** You can call Amtrak directly at **1-800-USA-RAIL** (1-800-872-7245) to have an agent book the ticket over the phone.\n\n*Tip: Because you are booking less than a week in advance, ticket prices may be higher than usual. Booking sooner rather than later will help you secure the best remaining fares.*",
